#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naimark's theorem"
msgstr "Teorema Naimark"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Naimark's theorem* is a fundamental fact concerning measurements.\n"
"It states that every general measurement can be implemented in a simple way that's reminiscent of Stinespring representations of channels:\n"
"1. The system to be measured is first combined with an initialized workspace system, forming a compound system.\n"
"2. A unitary operation is then performed on the compound system.\n"
"3. Finally, the workspace system is *measured* with respect to a *standard basis measurement*, yielding the outcome of the original general measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Teorema Naimark* adalah fakta fundamental tentang pengukuran.\n"
"Ini menyatakan bahwa setiap pengukuran umum dapat diimplementasikan dengan cara sederhana yang mengingatkan pada representasi Stinespring dari saluran:\n"
"1. Sistem yang akan diukur pertama kali digabungkan dengan sistem ruang kerja yang diinisialisasi, membentuk sistem gabungan.\n"
"2. Operasi uniter kemudian dilakukan pada sistem gabungan.\n"
"3. Akhirnya, sistem ruang kerja *diukur* terhadap *pengukuran basis standar*, menghasilkan hasil dari pengukuran umum asli.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement and proof {#theorem-statement-and-proof}"
msgstr "Pernyataan dan bukti teorema {#theorem-statement-and-proof}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let $\\mathsf{X}$ be a system and let $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ be a collection of positive semidefinite matrices satisfying\n"
msgstr "Misalkan $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah sistem dan misalkan $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ adalah koleksi matriks semidefinit positif yang memenuhi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is to say that they describe a measurement of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Also let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be a system whose classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, which is the set of possible outcomes of this measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"yang artinya mereka mendeskripsikan pengukuran dari $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Juga misalkan $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah sistem yang himpunan keadaan klasiknya adalah $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, yang merupakan himpunan kemungkinan hasil dari pengukuran ini.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naimark's theorem states that there exists a unitary operation $U$ on the compound system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ so that the implementation suggested by the following figure yields measurement outcomes that agree with the given measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$, meaning that the probabilities for the different possible measurement outcomes are precisely in agreement.\n"
msgstr "Teorema Naimark menyatakan bahwa ada operasi uniter $U$ pada sistem gabungan $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ sehingga implementasi yang disarankan oleh gambar berikut menghasilkan hasil pengukuran yang sesuai dengan pengukuran yang diberikan $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$, artinya probabilitas untuk kemungkinan hasil pengukuran yang berbeda persis sesuai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![An implementation of a general measurement as in Naimark's theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/general-measurements/Naimark.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Implementasi pengukuran umum seperti dalam teorema Naimark](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/general-measurements/Naimark.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, the system $\\mathsf{X}$ starts out in some arbitrary state $\\rho$ while $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state.\n"
"The unitary operation $U$ is applied to $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then the system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is measured with a standard basis measurement, yielding some outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk lebih jelasnya, sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ dimulai dalam beberapa keadaan arbitrer $\\rho$ sementara $\\mathsf{Y}$ diinisialisasi ke keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"Operasi uniter $U$ diterapkan ke $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ dan kemudian sistem $\\mathsf{Y}$ diukur dengan pengukuran basis standar, menghasilkan beberapa hasil $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The system $\\mathsf{X}$ is pictured as part of the output of the circuit, but for now we won't concern ourselves with the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ after $U$ is performed, and can imagine that it is traced out.\n"
"We'll be interested in the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ after $U$ is performed later in the lesson, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ digambarkan sebagai bagian dari output sirkuit, tetapi untuk saat ini kita tidak akan mempermasalahkan keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ setelah $U$ dilakukan, dan bisa membayangkan bahwa itu di-trace out.\n"
"Kita akan tertarik pada keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ setelah $U$ dilakukan nanti dalam pelajaran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An implementation of a measurement in this way is clearly reminiscent of a Stinespring representation of a channel, and the mathematical underpinnings are similar as well.\n"
"The difference here is that the workspace system is measured rather than being traced out like in the case of a Stinespring representation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Implementasi pengukuran dengan cara ini jelas mengingatkan pada representasi Stinespring dari saluran, dan dasar matematisnya serupa.\n"
"Perbedaannya di sini adalah bahwa sistem ruang kerja diukur daripada di-trace out seperti dalam kasus representasi Stinespring.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fact that every measurement can be implemented in this way is pretty simple to prove, but we're going to need a fact concerning positive semidefinite matrices first.\n"
msgstr "Fakta bahwa setiap pengukuran dapat diimplementasikan dengan cara ini cukup mudah dibuktikan, tetapi kita perlu fakta tentang matriks semidefinit positif terlebih dahulu.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Fact\">\n"
"Suppose $P$ is an $n \\times n$ positive semidefinite matrix. There exists a unique $n\\times n$ positive semidefinite matrix $Q$ for which $Q^2 = P$. This unique positive semidefinite matrix is called the *square root* of $P$ and is denoted $\\sqrt{P}$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Fakta\">\n"
"Misalkan $P$ adalah matriks semidefinit positif $n \\times n$. Ada matriks semidefinit positif $n\\times n$ unik $Q$ di mana $Q^2 = P$. Matriks semidefinit positif unik ini disebut *akar kuadrat* dari $P$ dan dinotasikan $\\sqrt{P}$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to find the square root of a positive semidefinite matrix is to first compute a spectral decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu cara untuk menemukan akar kuadrat dari matriks semidefinit positif adalah dengan pertama-tama menghitung dekomposisi spektral.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because $P$ is positive semidefinite, its eigenvalues must be nonnegative real numbers, and by replacing them with their square roots we obtain an expression for the square root of $P$.\n"
msgstr "Karena $P$ bersifat semidefinit positif, eigenvaluenya harus berupa bilangan real non-negatif, dan dengan menggantikannya dengan akar kuadratnya kita mendapatkan ekspresi untuk akar kuadrat $P$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{P} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{P} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this concept in hand, we're ready to prove Naimark's theorem.\n"
"Under the assumption that $\\mathsf{X}$ has $n$ classical states, a unitary operation $U$ on the pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ can be represented by an $nm\\times nm$ matrix, which we can view as an $m\\times m$ block matrix whose blocks are $n\\times n$.\n"
"The key to the proof is to take $U$ to be any unitary matrix that matches the following pattern.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan konsep ini di tangan, kita siap membuktikan teorema Naimark.\n"
"Dengan asumsi bahwa $\\mathsf{X}$ memiliki $n$ keadaan klasik, operasi uniter $U$ pada pasangan $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ dapat direpresentasikan oleh matriks $nm\\times nm$, yang bisa kita lihat sebagai matriks blok $m\\times m$ yang bloknya berukuran $n\\times n$.\n"
"Kunci pembuktian adalah mengambil $U$ sebagai matriks uniter manapun yang cocok dengan pola berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For it to be possible to fill in the blocks marked with a question mark so that $U$ is unitary, it's both necessary and sufficient that the first $n$ columns, which are formed by the blocks $\\sqrt{P_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}$, are orthonormal.\n"
"We can then use the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to fill in the remaining columns, just like we encountered in the previous lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agar mungkin mengisi blok-blok yang ditandai dengan tanda tanya sehingga $U$ uniter, syarat yang diperlukan dan cukup adalah bahwa $n$ kolom pertama, yang dibentuk oleh blok $\\sqrt{P_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}$, bersifat ortonormal.\n"
"Kita kemudian bisa menggunakan proses ortonormalisasi Gram-Schmidt untuk mengisi kolom-kolom yang tersisa, seperti yang kita temui dalam pelajaran sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first $n$ columns of $U$ can be expressed as vectors in the following way, where $c = 0,\\ldots,n-1$ refers to the column number starting from $0$.\n"
msgstr "$n$ kolom pertama dari $U$ dapat dinyatakan sebagai vektor dengan cara berikut, di mana $c = 0,\\ldots,n-1$ mengacu pada nomor kolom mulai dari $0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_c\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\vert c\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_c\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\vert c\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can compute the inner product between any two of them as follows.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menghitung hasil kali dalam antara dua di antaranya sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_c \\vert \\gamma_d \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle \\cdot \\langle c \\vert \\sqrt{P_a}\\sqrt{P_b}\\, \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a \\Biggr) \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_c \\vert \\gamma_d \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle \\cdot \\langle c \\vert \\sqrt{P_a}\\sqrt{P_b}\\, \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a \\Biggr) \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This shows that these columns are in fact orthonormal, so we can fill in the remaining columns of $U$ in a way that guarantees the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr "Ini menunjukkan bahwa kolom-kolom ini sebenarnya bersifat ortonormal, sehingga kita bisa mengisi kolom-kolom yang tersisa dari $U$ dengan cara yang menjamin seluruh matriks adalah uniter.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to check that the measurement outcome probabilities for the simulation are consistent with the original measurement.\n"
"For a given initial state $\\rho$ of $\\mathsf{X}$, the measurement described by the collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ results in each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang tersisa adalah memeriksa bahwa probabilitas hasil pengukuran untuk simulasi konsisten dengan pengukuran aslinya.\n"
"Untuk keadaan awal $\\rho$ dari $\\mathsf{X}$, pengukuran yang dijelaskan oleh koleksi $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ menghasilkan setiap hasil $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ dengan probabilitas $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To obtain the outcome probabilities for the simulation, let's first give the name $\\sigma$ to the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ after $U$ has been performed.\n"
"This state can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mendapatkan probabilitas hasil untuk simulasi, mari kita beri nama $\\sigma$ untuk keadaan $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ setelah $U$ dilakukan.\n"
"Keadaan ini dapat dinyatakan sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalently, in a block matrix form, we have the following equation.\n"
msgstr "Setara, dalam bentuk matriks blok, kita memiliki persamaan berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sigma & =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\rho & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\sqrt{P_1} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sigma & =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\rho & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\sqrt{P_1} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that the entries of $U$ falling into the blocks marked with a question mark have no influence on the outcome by virtue of the fact that we're conjugating a matrix of the form $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$\n"
"— so the question mark entries are always multiplied by zero entries of $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ when the matrix product is computed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa entri $U$ yang jatuh ke dalam blok yang ditandai dengan tanda tanya tidak berpengaruh pada hasilnya karena kita mengkonjugasikan matriks berbentuk $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$\n"
"— sehingga entri tanda tanya selalu dikalikan dengan entri nol dari $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ ketika perkalian matriks dihitung.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can analyze what happens when a standard basis measurement is performed on $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"The probabilities of the possible outcomes are given by the diagonal entries of the reduced state $\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}}$ of $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita bisa menganalisis apa yang terjadi ketika pengukuran basis standar dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Probabilitas dari kemungkinan hasil diberikan oleh entri diagonal dari keadaan tereduksi $\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}}$ dari $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} = \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\\Bigr) \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} = \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\\Bigr) \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, using the cyclic property of the trace, we see that the probability to obtain a given outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ is as follows.\n"
msgstr "Khususnya, menggunakan sifat siklik dari jejak, kita melihat bahwa probabilitas untuk mendapatkan hasil tertentu $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}\\Bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}\\Bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This matches with the original measurement, establishing the correctness of the simulation.\n"
msgstr "Ini cocok dengan pengukuran aslinya, membuktikan kebenaran simulasi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-destructive measurements {#non-destructive-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran non-destruktif {#non-destructive-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So far in the lesson, we've concerned ourselves with *destructive* measurements, where the output consists of the classical measurement result alone and there is no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of the system that was measured.\n"
msgstr "Sejauh ini dalam pelajaran, kita telah mempermasalahkan pengukuran *destruktif*, di mana outputnya hanya terdiri dari hasil pengukuran klasik saja dan tidak ada spesifikasi tentang keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran dari sistem yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Non-destructive* measurements, on the other hand, do precisely this.\n"
"Specifically, non-destructive measurements describe not only the classical measurement outcome probabilities, but also the state of the system that was measured conditioned on each possible measurement outcome.\n"
"Note that the term *non-destructive* refers to the *system* being measured but not necessarily its state, which could change significantly as a result of the measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengukuran *non-destruktif*, di sisi lain, melakukan hal ini dengan tepat.\n"
"Secara khusus, pengukuran non-destruktif mendeskripsikan bukan hanya probabilitas hasil pengukuran klasik, tetapi juga keadaan sistem yang diukur yang dikondisikan pada setiap kemungkinan hasil pengukuran.\n"
"Perhatikan bahwa istilah *non-destruktif* mengacu pada *sistem* yang diukur tetapi tidak harus keadaannya, yang bisa berubah secara signifikan sebagai akibat dari pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, for a given destructive measurement, there will be multiple (in fact infinitely many) non-destructive measurements that are *compatible* with the given destructive measurement, meaning that the classical measurement outcome probabilities match precisely with the destructive measurement.\n"
"So, there isn't a unique way to define the post-measurement quantum state of a system for a given measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara umum, untuk pengukuran destruktif yang diberikan, akan ada beberapa (faktanya tak terbatas banyaknya) pengukuran non-destruktif yang *kompatibel* dengan pengukuran destruktif yang diberikan, artinya probabilitas hasil pengukuran klasik cocok persis dengan pengukuran destruktif.\n"
"Jadi, tidak ada cara unik untuk mendefinisikan keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran dari suatu sistem untuk pengukuran yang diberikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is, in fact, possible to generalize non-destructive measurements even further, so that they produce a classical measurement outcome along with a quantum state output of a system that isn't necessarily the same as the input system.\n"
msgstr "Sebenarnya memungkinkan untuk menggeneralisasi pengukuran non-destruktif lebih jauh, sehingga mereka menghasilkan hasil pengukuran klasik bersama dengan keadaan kuantum keluaran dari sistem yang tidak harus sama dengan sistem input.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a non-destructive measurement is an interesting and useful abstraction.\n"
"It should, however, be recognized that non-destructive measurements can always be described as compositions of channels and destructive measurements — so there is a sense in which the notion of a destructive measurement is the more fundamental one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagasan pengukuran non-destruktif adalah abstraksi yang menarik dan berguna.\n"
"Namun, harus diakui bahwa pengukuran non-destruktif selalu dapat digambarkan sebagai komposisi dari saluran dan pengukuran destruktif — sehingga ada pengertian di mana gagasan pengukuran destruktif adalah yang lebih fundamental.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "From Naimark's theorem {#from-naimarks-theorem}"
msgstr "Dari teorema Naimark {#from-naimarks-theorem}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the simulation of a general measurement like we have in Naimark's theorem.\n"
"A simple way to obtain a non-destructive measurement from this simulation is revealed by the figure from before, where the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is not traced out, but is part of the output.\n"
"This yields both a classical measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ as well as a post-measurement quantum state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan simulasi pengukuran umum seperti yang kita miliki dalam teorema Naimark.\n"
"Cara sederhana untuk mendapatkan pengukuran non-destruktif dari simulasi ini terungkap dari gambar sebelumnya, di mana sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ tidak di-trace out, tetapi merupakan bagian dari output.\n"
"Ini menghasilkan baik hasil pengukuran klasik $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ maupun keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran dari $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's describe these states in mathematical terms.\n"
"We're assuming that the initial state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\rho$, so that after the initialized system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is introduced and $U$ is performed, we have that $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ is in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita deskripsikan keadaan-keadaan ini dalam istilah matematis.\n"
"Kita mengasumsikan bahwa keadaan awal $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah $\\rho$, sehingga setelah sistem $\\mathsf{Y}$ yang diinisialisasi diperkenalkan dan $U$ dilakukan, kita memiliki bahwa $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ berada dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probabilities for the different classical outcomes to appear are the same as before — they can't change as a result of us deciding to ignore or not ignore $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"That is, we obtain each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Probabilitas untuk hasil klasik yang berbeda muncul adalah sama seperti sebelumnya — mereka tidak bisa berubah sebagai akibat dari kita memutuskan untuk mengabaikan atau tidak mengabaikan $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Artinya, kita mendapatkan setiap $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ dengan probabilitas $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conditioned upon having obtained a particular measurement outcome $a$, the resulting state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is given by this expression.\n"
msgstr "Dikondisikan pada mendapatkan hasil pengukuran tertentu $a$, keadaan yang dihasilkan dari $\\mathsf{X}$ diberikan oleh ekspresi ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to see this is to represent a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ by the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m$, where the channel output describes classical measurement outcomes as (diagonal) density matrices.\n"
"An expression of the state we obtain is as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu cara untuk melihat ini adalah dengan merepresentasikan pengukuran basis standar dari $\\mathsf{Y}$ dengan saluran dephasing sempurna $\\Delta_m$, di mana output saluran mendeskripsikan hasil pengukuran klasik sebagai matriks densitas (diagonal).\n"
"Ekspresi dari keadaan yang kita peroleh adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\Delta_m(\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert) \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"= \\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\Delta_m(\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert) \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"= \\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can then write this state as a convex combination of product states,\n"
msgstr "Kita kemudian bisa menulis keadaan ini sebagai kombinasi konveks dari keadaan produk,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\\, \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\\, \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is consistent with the expression we've obtained for the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on each possible measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr "yang konsisten dengan ekspresi yang kita peroleh untuk keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ yang dikondisikan pada setiap kemungkinan hasil pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "From a Kraus representation {#from-a-kraus-representation}"
msgstr "Dari representasi Kraus {#from-a-kraus-representation}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are alternative selections for $U$ in the context of Naimark's theorem that produce the same measurement outcome probabilities but give entirely different output states of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "Ada pilihan alternatif untuk $U$ dalam konteks teorema Naimark yang menghasilkan probabilitas hasil pengukuran yang sama tetapi memberikan keadaan output $\\mathsf{X}$ yang sepenuhnya berbeda.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For instance, one option is to substitute $(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes V) U$ for $U$, where $V$ is any unitary operation on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"The application of $V$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ commutes with the measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ so the classical outcome probabilities do not change, but now the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on the outcome $a$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, satu opsi adalah menggantikan $(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes V) U$ untuk $U$, di mana $V$ adalah operasi uniter manapun pada $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Penerapan $V$ ke $\\mathsf{X}$ komut dengan pengukuran $\\mathsf{Y}$ sehingga probabilitas hasil klasik tidak berubah, tetapi sekarang keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ yang dikondisikan pada hasil $a$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, we could replace $U$ by the unitary matrix\n"
msgstr "Lebih umumnya, kita bisa menggantikan $U$ dengan matriks uniter\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert \\otimes V_a\\Biggr) U\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert \\otimes V_a\\Biggr) U\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any choice of unitary operations $V_0,\\ldots,V_{m-1}$ on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Again, the classical outcome probabilities are unchanged, but now the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on the outcome $a$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk pilihan operasi uniter $V_0,\\ldots,V_{m-1}$ manapun pada $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Sekali lagi, probabilitas hasil klasik tidak berubah, tetapi sekarang keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ yang dikondisikan pada hasil $a$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V_a \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V_a \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An equivalent way to express this freedom is connected with Kraus representations.\n"
"That is, we can describe an $m$-outcome non-destructive measurement of a system having $n$ classical states by a selection of $n\\times n$ Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ satisfying the typical condition for Kraus matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara setara untuk mengekspresikan kebebasan ini terhubung dengan representasi Kraus.\n"
"Artinya, kita bisa mendeskripsikan pengukuran non-destruktif $m$-hasil dari sistem dengan $n$ keadaan klasik dengan memilih $n\\times n$ matriks Kraus $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ yang memenuhi kondisi tipikal untuk matriks Kraus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} A_a^{\\dagger} A_a = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} A_a^{\\dagger} A_a = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assuming that the initial state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\rho$, the classical measurement outcome is $a$ with probability\n"
msgstr "Dengan asumsi bahwa keadaan awal $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah $\\rho$, hasil pengukuran klasiknya adalah $a$ dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a^{\\dagger} A_a \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a^{\\dagger} A_a \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and conditioned upon the outcome being $a$ the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "dan dikondisikan pada hasilnya adalah $a$, keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(A_a^{\\dagger}A_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(A_a^{\\dagger}A_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this is equivalent to choosing the unitary operation $U$ in Naimark's theorem as follows.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa ini setara dengan memilih operasi uniter $U$ dalam teorema Naimark sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson we observed that the columns formed by the blocks $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ are necessarily orthogonal, by virtue of the\n"
"condition $(1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran sebelumnya kita mengamati bahwa kolom yang dibentuk oleh blok $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ pasti ortogonal, berdasarkan\n"
"kondisi $(1)$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generalizations {#generalizations}"
msgstr "Generalisasi {#generalizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are even more general ways to formulate non-destructive measurements than the ways we've discussed.\n"
"The notion of a *quantum instrument* (which won't be described here) represents one way to do this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada cara yang bahkan lebih umum untuk memformulasikan pengukuran non-destruktif daripada cara yang sudah kita bahas.\n"
"Gagasan tentang *instrumen kuantum* (yang tidak akan dijelaskan di sini) mewakili salah satu cara untuk melakukannya.\n"
